 _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS fsck_tracker_health.py:256-277, and fsck_scan.py inline `issues += 1`","No shared registry exists (search for is_issue shows only per-site decisions)"],"finding":"The plan calls _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS 'single-sourced as a module constant' but it is actually a SECOND, hand-maintained enumeration of the is_issue=False decisions, which live at three independent production sites (the _tracker_health tuple at fsck_tracker_health.py:60-66, _DIRTY_LINE_SPECS at :256-277, and inline `issues += 1` in fsck_scan.py). Since the exit-code tally derives from those flags while JSON counted-ness derives from _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS, a future is_issue=False kind added at a production site would update the exit code (via _scan) but NOT the constant — silently reintroducing the very count-disagreement this plan fixes (the new kind gets counted=true and re-inflates issue_count).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd44d9a6105b8b2f2","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan step 1 (fsck.py _transform_json, _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS)","norm_id":"n333b342da85572c8","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A maintainer adds a new report-only (is_issue=False) tracker check next year, wires it into _tracker_health with is_issue=False, but forgets to add its JSON kind to _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS — the disagreement silently returns for that kind"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a RED cross-check test that derives the is_issue=False kind set from the production sources (_DIRTY_LINE_SPECS + the _tracker_health pairs + the fsck_scan report-only lines) and asserts it equals _NEVER_COUNTED_KINDS, so any new never-counted kind that forgets the constant fails a test rather than silently diverging.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_u